# Reference Point — Gap Card Headline (`h3` in `.gap-card`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for a gap/problem card headline (e.g. "Confidence ends at checkout"), match plain `h3` inside `.gap-card` in `#problem`.

## Structure

```html
<article class="gap-card">
  <p class="g-label">Returns feel risky on high-value items</p>
  <h3>Confidence ends at checkout</h3>
  <hr /><p class="lead">Returning a ₹50,000 piece feels uncertain.</p>
</article>
```

Use a plain `h3` — no `.title`, `.display`, or extra classes.

## Visual spec

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `h3` (no class) inside `.gap-card` |
| Font | `var(--serif)` (Instrument Serif) |
| Size | `var(--h3)` → `clamp(1.15rem, 1.6vw, 1.5rem)` |
| Weight | `400` |
| Style | **italic** |
| Color | `var(--ink)` |
| Line-height | `1.1` (from base `h3`) |

## Full gap card stack

1. `.g-label` — muted brown uppercase label
2. **`h3`** — italic serif headline ← this reference
3. `hr` — divider
4. `.lead` — grey body copy

## vs other headlines

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `h3` in `.gap-card` | Card punchline — italic, compact |
| `h3.title` | Subsection heads — not italic, `--title-sm` |
| `.display` | Main section heads — larger, not italic |
| `.compare-side .claim` | Comparison VS callout — similar italic serif, `1.05rem` |

## Do not

- Add `.title` or `.display` to gap card headlines.
- Use sans-serif or remove italic.
- Use `<h2>` — keep `h3` for card-level hierarchy.
